From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 21:56:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02682/11362] [outer-loop] Repeated-seed grounding rate settles
 it: base Qwen3.5-9B-MTP 62.5% vs DeepSeek-Flash 25% -- base wins, raise cap
 to >=2048

Operator: run base vs DeepSeek-Flash 3-5x each + raise the token cap (truncation check). Ran 4 seeds x
ka59+tn36, MTP on, n_predict 2560:
  base Qwen3.5-9B-MTP:    ka59 3/4 + tn36 2/4 = 5/8 (62.5%)
  DeepSeek-V4-Flash-MTP:  ka59 1/4 + tn36 1/4 = 2/8 (25%)
Base grounds 2.5x more often -- DeepSeek-Flash distill is faster (90% MTP accept, 17.8 tok/s) but clearly
LESS accurate, writing wrong/verbose rules more often (hit the 2560 cap on 3/8 runs -> not just truncation).
Cap finding confirmed: base went 1/2 -> 3/4 on ka59 with 2 grounding runs needing >1100 tokens, so the old
1100 cap WAS truncating real solves -> deploy with n_predict >= ~2048. Final stack: base Qwen3.5-9B-MTP +
8-bit KV + n_predict>=2048. New driver arc3_layerb_repeat_bench.py (grounding-rate over seeds).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
